completed_at: "2026-08-08T07:59:16.848Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Every Sentry event the CLI captures carries pm.error_code and pm.exit_code tags, set at capture time and independent of whether a command span is active; An error with no declared code is tagged with an explicit unclassified sentinel rather than no tag, so the gate always has a value to judge; A negative control proves an error raised before any command span still arrives tagged; The release gate's fail-closed branch can no longer be reached by a CLI-produced event, and a test asserts producer/consumer contract parity against the declared catalog"
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "sentryCaptureCliError now attaches pm.error_code and pm.exit_code to the captured event itself, independent of any active command span, with an unclassified_runtime_error sentinel for undeclared faults."
expected_result: "Every CLI-produced Sentry event carries the contract the release gate reads, so the gate's fail-closed branch is unreachable for lack of metadata while still blocking genuine unclassified defects."
actual_result: Tags are set at capture time for span and no-span paths; undeclared faults tag the sentinel and still block; Node errno codes are not promoted to pm codes; 43 sentry-helper tests pass.
