comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-08T07:58:24.554Z","harness:claude-code","Root cause confirmed against the 2026-08-08 scheduled cut (run 31238168668). The gate read pm.error_code/pm.exit_code from Sentry issue tags and failed closed; both blocking events (PM-CLI-2S, PM-CLI-2Q) carried handled=yes and neither tag. sentryCaptureCliError put exit_code only into event extras, and the sole tag writer (setSentryCommandFinishTags via sentryFinishCommandSpan) begins with an early return when no command span is active — so the unknown-error path captured before the writer ran, and any pre-span failure never reached it at all. Fix attaches the contract to the event itself at capture time. An undeclared fault now tags unclassified_runtime_error, which resolves to no catalog contract and therefore still blocks, so fail-closed is preserved for real defects while becoming reachable-by-construction rather than unsatisfiable. A Node errno error (string code, no numeric exitCode) is deliberately not promoted to a pm code. Evidence: 43 sentry-helper tests pass including a no-active-span negative control."
